From aba0f922b in plasma/breeze (Plasma/6.7 branch)
Subject: [PATCH 3] SE_ItemViewItemText: take the horizontal inset only from
 space the text does not need

Third alternative, alongside patches 0001 and 0002. Neither of those is
conditional: 0001 removes the inset outright, 0002 removes half of it. This one
keeps the inset wherever the item is wide enough to spare it, and yields it only
where taking it would elide text that would otherwise have fitted.

Applies to Qt5 and Qt6 alike. No version conditional is introduced: breeze5.so
and breeze6.so are built from one translation unit, and the guard is a function
of available width, not of Qt major version.

Why the comparison is not against rect.width()
----------------------------------------------
QCommonStylePrivate::viewItemDrawText() removes PM_FocusFrameHMargin + 1 from
each side of whatever subElementRect() returned, immediately before eliding:

    QRect textRect = rect.adjusted(textMargin, 0, -textMargin, 0);

A guard that compared the string against rect.width() would therefore conclude
that the text fits, keep the full inset, and still leave the label short by
2 * textMargin. The value is obtained through proxy()->pixelMetric(), which is
the same source QCommonStyle uses, so the two agree by construction rather than
by coincidence.

Behaviour, measured (plasma-breeze-6.7.3-2.fc43.1, Qt 5.15.18 / 6.10.3)
----------------------------------------------------------------------
  parent rect   available   required   inset applied   result
  Qt6, 400px          394        188         6 (full)   unchanged from stock
  Qt6, 200px          194        188         6 (full)   fits; no elision
  Qt5, 400px          188        188         0          equivalent to patch 0001
  Qt5, 150px          144        188         0          equivalent to patch 0001

On Qt 5.15 the text rect arrives already clamped to the string's natural size,
because QCommonStylePrivate::viewItemLayout() bounds it when
showDecorationSelected is false, which is what Breeze's style hint reports.
There is consequently never slack to preserve on Qt5 and the guard yields the
whole inset, matching patch 0001. On Qt6 that clamp was removed, so the guard
preserves the inset in every view wide enough not to need it.

Excluded cases
--------------
  Qt::ElideNone            the text is clipped rather than elided; the guard
                           would not prevent anything, so the inset is kept
  WrapText                 horizontalAdvance() of the whole string does not
                           describe wrapped text, so the inset is kept

In both, and where the option carries no text, behaviour is identical to stock.

Metrics at Plasma/6.7.3, for reference:
  ItemView_ItemMarginLeft/Right  2px each, reduced to 1px each by
                                 Helper::itemViewItemMargins() when the view is
                                 a QFrame::StyledPanel, which item views are
  ItemView_ItemPaddingWidth      2px
  => 3px per side in a framed view, 6px total; 4px per side unframed, 8px total

--- a/kstyle/breezestyle.cpp
+++ b/kstyle/breezestyle.cpp
@@ -1062,8 +1062,32 @@
         QRect rect = ParentStyleClass::subElementRect(element, option, widget);
         if (viewItem) {
             const QMargins margins = _helper->itemViewItemMargins(viewItem);
-            rect.setRight(rect.right() - margins.right() - Metrics::ItemView_ItemPaddingWidth);
-            rect.setLeft(rect.left() + margins.left() + Metrics::ItemView_ItemPaddingWidth);
+            const int leftInset = margins.left() + Metrics::ItemView_ItemPaddingWidth;
+            const int rightInset = margins.right() + Metrics::ItemView_ItemPaddingWidth;
+
+            // Take the inset only out of space the text does not need. Where the
+            // item is wide enough to spare it, the full inset is applied exactly
+            // as before; where it is not, the text keeps the width it needs
+            // rather than being elided by the inset itself.
+            //
+            // The comparison must be made against the width the text is really
+            // laid out in, not against rect.width(): QCommonStylePrivate::
+            // viewItemDrawText() removes PM_FocusFrameHMargin + 1 from each side
+            // again, after this function has returned.
+            int inset = leftInset + rightInset;
+            if (viewItem->textElideMode != Qt::ElideNone && !(viewItem->features & QStyleOptionViewItem::WrapText)) {
+                const int textMargin = proxy()->pixelMetric(PM_FocusFrameHMargin, option, widget) + 1;
+                const int available = rect.width() - 2 * textMargin;
+                const int required = viewItem->fontMetrics.horizontalAdvance(viewItem->text);
+                inset = qBound(0, available - required, inset);
+            }
+
+            // Split what remains in the original proportion, so a reduced inset
+            // keeps the text positioned as it would have been.
+            const int total = leftInset + rightInset;
+            const int right = total > 0 ? inset * rightInset / total : 0;
+            rect.setRight(rect.right() - right);
+            rect.setLeft(rect.left() + (inset - right));
             rect.moveTop(rect.top() + margins.top() - margins.bottom());
         }
 
